  "idea": "How to schedule emails to send at a later date and time automatically",
  "text": "Write your work messages whenever you want, but deliver them whenever it is actually best. Working during your peak night hours tempts you to hit send, creating messy after-hours communication. Random midnight notifications annoy colleagues, blur your boundaries, and invite stressful late-night message threads. Hit the Schedule Send arrow in Outlook or Gmail to dispatch messages tomorrow morning at eight. You maintain complete control over your working schedule.",
